# Folder-level sensitivity rules. One rule per line:  <glob> = private|secret
# Blank lines and #-comments are ignored. The glob is matched against the
# VAULT-RELATIVE path, as a shell case pattern, so `*` also crosses `/`
# (`Journal/*` covers every subfolder). `**` is accepted and means the same.
#
# A note's own frontmatter (`sensitivity: private|secret`) counts too; the
# stricter of the two wins. No rule and no frontmatter = normal.
#
#   private  indexed; search returns a pointer unless the session opts in
#            (AIOS_INCLUDE_PRIVATE=1); Read asks first
#   secret   as private, plus secret values are redacted in the index and
#            search never returns its text
#
# Read by guard-sensitive-read.sh and by the search index. Never exported:
# your folder names describe your vault.
#
# Examples:
# Journal/* = private
# Therapy/* = private
